                Stopping Mirroring
                ------------------

                To stop mirroring -- you will need to do this before
                backing up a mirrored LD -- issue the ?RELEASE system call.

                Should one of the disks containing an LD image suffer a
                hardware error, AOS/VS II automatically stops mirroring for
                you.  AOS/VS "breaks" the mirror by removing the "bad"
                image, while still allowing you to run on the good image.
                AOS/VS, in turn, sends messages to the error file and the
                system console indicating that it has broken the mirror.

	|	Getting Mirror Status Information
                ---------------------------------

	|	AOS/VS II Release 1.00 does not include the AOS/VS program
	|	:UTIL:MIRRORINFO.PR.  DGC will provide a mechanism in a
	|	future release to get mirror status information.  In the
	|	meantime, you can get status information when you initialize
	|	a mirror.  The return from the INITIALIZE command indicates
	|	whether the images are synchronized or not.


